صَلِّ يَا رَبِّ عَلَى عَالِي ذُرَى / سُودَدِ أَفْضَلِ مَنْ دَاسَ الثَّرَى
Ṣalli yā rabbi ʿalā ʿālī dhurā / sūdadi afḍali man dāsa th-tharā
Bless, O my Lord, the one who stands atop the heights of sovereignty — the best of all who ever trod the earth.



يَا حَبِيبَ اللهِ يَا خَيْرَ الوَرَى / يَا رَفِيعَ القَدْرِ أَسْمَى مَنْ سَرَى
Yā ḥabība llāhi yā khayra l-warā / yā rafīʿa l-qadri asmā man sarā
O Beloved of God, O best of creation, O you of lofty worth, highest of all who journeyed by night.



فِيكَ قَدْ عَزَّ وَضِيعُ القَدْرِ يَا / سَيِّدَ السَّادَاتِ يَا ذُخْرَ الوَرَى
Fīka qad ʿazza waḍīʿu l-qadri yā / sayyida s-sādāti yā dhukhra l-warā
Through you the man of lowly standing is made honourable — O master of masters, O treasure of creation.



وَاعْتَلَا ذِرْوَةَ مَجْدٍ وَارْتَقَى / مُرْتَقَى مَنْ كَانَ ذَا رُشْدٍ دَرَى
Wa-ʿtalā dhirwata majdin wa-rtaqā / murtaqā man kāna dhā rushdin darā
He climbed to the summit of glory and ascended the ascent of one rightly guided and knowing.



وَاكْتَسَى فِي ظَاهِرٍ ثَوْبَ العُلَا / مِثْلَ وَالٍ وَأَمِيرٍ أُمِّرَا
Wa-ktasā fī ẓāhirin thawba l-ʿulā / mithla wālin wa-amīrin ummirā
Outwardly he was clothed in the garment of eminence, like a governor, or a prince given command.



وَارْتَدَى بِالجَاهِ ثُمَّ السُّودَدِ / وَوَقَارٍ مِثْلَ مَا مِنْ عَبْقَرَا
Wa-rtadā bi-l-jāhi thumma s-sūdadi / wa waqārin mithla mā min ʿabqarā
He wrapped himself in high standing, then in mastery, and in a gravity like something out of ʿAbqar.



كَعَظِيمٍ أَوْ حَبِيبٍ حَبَّهُ / أَهْلُ فَضْلٍ وَاحْتِرَامٍ وَائْتَرَى
Ka-ʿaẓīmin aw ḥabībin ḥabbahu / ahlu faḍlin wa-ḥtirāmin wa-ʾtarā
Like some great one, or a beloved whom the people of virtue and reverence have loved and chosen for themselves.



وَبِأَصْلٍ ثُمَّ فَرْعٍ مُؤْمِنٍ / وَبِمَنْ أَوْصَى لَنَا وَالفُقَرَا
Wa bi-aṣlin thumma farʿin muʾminin / wa bi-man awṣā lanā wa-l-fuqarā
And by a believing root and branch alike, and by the one who left his counsel to us and to the poor.



فَعَلَيْكَ اللهُ صَلَّى دَائِمًا / مَا دَجَا لَيْلٌ وَمَا سَارٍ سَرَى
Fa-ʿalayka llāhu ṣallā dāʾiman / mā dajā laylun wa mā sārin sarā
So may God bless you perpetually, as long as night falls dark and as long as any traveller journeys on